{
  "_readme": [
    "Little Thing of Nowa, ep.03 — why Nowa is a virtual pet raising game.",
    "",
    "The argument: what game should sit on this hardware? → Tamagotchi stood out → the",
    "2000s were the dopamine era, Tamagotchi wasn't → a Bandai designer wanted a pet for",
    "people who couldn't have one → 100 million units → the loop is slow and frankly",
    "annoying: feed it, play with it, put it to bed → caring costs you time, effort, money",
    "and gives nothing back → and that is exactly why it worked: care becomes",
    "responsibility becomes attachment → so that is the gameplay we reimagined → and the",
    "pet still doesn't speak human, for the reasons in ep.02.",
    "",
    "Presentation: this is the longest episode, so it spends the layout library — 21",
    "distinct presentations, no type-layout pair twice. The Tamagotchi beats use `plate`",
    "scenes with CC-BY photographs from Wikimedia, credited on screen from the manifest.",
    "",
    "IP: the Tamagotchi PHOTOGRAPHS are CC BY (credited). The DEVICE is Bandai's product",
    "design, shown editorially while discussing its design history. Flagged for human",
    "sign-off before publishing — set approved:false in media/sources.json to pull them."
  ],
